      "writtenOn": "2024-03-16T01:19:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`source_module_name` defaults to the naming convention of the module name without the `prebuilt_` prefix. If we do not explicitly specify the `source_module_name` in `prebuilt_myconfig.v2`, then its `source_module_name` will be `myconfig.v2`\n\n\u003e  How would the expected testing behavior differ when myconfig.v2 did not specify the source_module_name property?\n\nIn this scenario, two soong modules will have enabled\u003dtrue, and therefore the singleton [platform_compat_config_singleton](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/build/soong/+/7d53941629b5e7112ad4658c59dea1ac58a7cd6b:java/platform_compat_config.go;l\u003d225-236;drc\u003d8ff105860d20f2ccbb8d8044bf562f94100b7f6a;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0) will merge two .xml files.",
      "parentUuid": "e1e03b06_1c9990df",
      "revId": "dc1bdd97cd0872ae94f428373c025b5be17a190a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9ab2a5f_630b1fcf",
        "filename": "java/java_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2689,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-16T01:33:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In this scenario, two soong modules will have enabled\u003dtrue, and therefore the singleton platform_compat_config_singleton will merge two .xml files.\n\nAcknowledged, do you mind adding a comment regarding this here?\n\nOne follow up question (for my own benefit to better understand the multiple prebuilts):\n- Are multiple `prebuilt_myconfig.v*` modules allowed to set the same `source_module_name`? If not, is there a mechanism to prevent it?",
      "parentUuid": "d7865e7e_4f63c373",
      "revId": "dc1bdd97cd0872ae94f428373c025b5be17a190a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
